Here's the updated README.doctor with generic project names:

```doctor
title# Doctor Documentation

hero# Doctor
desc# A single-file documentation language that compiles to GitHub Pages HTML.

sidebar# Quick Start | #quick-start
sidebar# Installation | #installation
sidebar# Your First File | #first-file
sidebar# Syntax | #syntax
sidebar# Advanced | #advanced
sidebar# Setup | #setup
sidebar# Troubleshooting | #troubleshooting
sidebar# Examples | #examples

h2# Quick Start

list#
- Create docs/index.doctor
- Write your content
- Push to GitHub
- Your site is live
end#

h2# Installation

p# Doctor requires no installation. It runs entirely through GitHub Actions.

h3# What You Need

list#
- A GitHub account
- A repository
- One .doctor file in a docs/ folder
end#

h3# Repository Setup

code# text
your-repo/
├── .github/workflows/build.yml
├── docs/
│   └── index.doctor
├── doctor.py
└── _config.yml
end#

h2# Your First Doctor File

p# Create docs/index.doctor:

code# doctor
title# Prism Docs

hero# Prism
desc# A documentation site built with Doctor.

h2# What is Doctor?

p# Doctor is a single-file markup language that compiles to GitHub Pages HTML. No complex setup. No local build tools. Just write and push.
end#

p# Commit and push. GitHub Actions will compile this to HTML and deploy it.

h2# Syntax Reference

h3# Title

p# Sets the page title.

code# doctor
title# My Documentation Site
end#

h3# Hero

p# A large heading with optional description.

code# doctor
hero# Prism
desc# We build things that work.
end#

h3# Headings

p# Three levels of headings.

code# doctor
h1# Main Heading
h2# Section Heading
h3# Subsection Heading
end#

h3# Paragraphs

p# Simple text blocks.

code# doctor
p# This is a paragraph of text.
end#

h3# Sidebar

p# Navigation links for the left sidebar.

code# doctor
sidebar# Getting Started | #start
sidebar# Components | #components
sidebar# API Reference | #api
end#

h3# Tables

p# Structured data with headers and rows.

code# doctor
table# Project | Year | Status
Project A | 2025 | Active
Project B | 2024 | Archived
end#

h3# Lists

p# Bullet lists.

code# doctor
list#
- Product design
- Frontend engineering
end#
end#

h3# Code Blocks

p# Syntax-highlighted snippets.

code# doctor
code# python
def hello():
    print("Hello Doctor")
end#
end#

h3# Alerts

p# Contextual messages with emoji indicators.

code# doctor
alert# info
p# This feature requires v2.0+

alert# warning
p# Breaking change in next release
end#

alert# tip
p# Available types: info, warning, success, error, tip

h3# Cards

p# Title and description blocks.

code# doctor
card# The Classic
desc# Acetate frames, timeless design
end#

h3# Dividers

p# Horizontal rules for separating sections.

code# doctor
divider#
end#

h3# Images

p# Embed images with source and alt text.

code# doctor
img# ./assets/hero.jpg|Hero banner
end#

h3# Grids

p# Group cards in a grid layout.

code# doctor
grid#
card# Fast
desc# Compiles in seconds
end#
end#

h2# Advanced Usage

h3# Custom Landing Pages

p# Create an index.html in your repo root. The workflow must preserve it.

h3# File Structure

h3# Minimal Setup

code# text
your-repo/
├── .github/workflows/build.yml
├── docs/
│   └── index.doctor
├── doctor.py
└── _config.yml
end#

h3# Full Setup

code# text
your-repo/
├── .github/workflows/build.yml
├── docs/
│   └── index.doctor
├── index.html
├── showcase.html
├── doctor.py
├── _config.yml
└── assets/
    └── images/
end#

h2# GitHub Pages Setup

list#
- Go to Settings → Pages in your repo
- Under Build and deployment, select GitHub Actions
- Save
end#

h2# Troubleshooting

h3# 404 Error

alert# error
p# Cause: Missing index.html or index.md at site root.
end#

p# Fix: Ensure doctor.py outputs docs/index.md and Jekyll builds it, or provide a custom index.html.

h3# Build Fails

alert# error
p# Cause: Workflow step exits with error.
end#

p# Fix: Add || echo fallbacks to all run steps so failures do not block deployment.

h3# Images Do Not Show

alert# error
p# Cause: Wrong path or missing file.
end#

p# Fix: Use relative paths, upload images to repo, or use external URLs.

h2# Examples

h3# Documentation Site

code# doctor
title# API Documentation

hero# REST API
desc# Complete reference for developers.

sidebar# Authentication | #auth
sidebar# Endpoints | #endpoints

h2# Authentication

p# All requests require a Bearer token.

code# bash
curl -H "Authorization: Bearer TOKEN" \
  https://api.example.com/v1/users
end#

alert# warning
p# Tokens expire after 24 hours.
end#

h2# Endpoints

table# Method | Endpoint | Description
GET | /users | List all users
POST | /users | Create user
end#
end#

